WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.830
- [Narrator] This is no ordinary rabbit.

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:05.570
This is the New England cottontail-

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:09.221
a species that's been pushed
to the limits of its survival.

00:00:09.221 --> 00:00:12.304
(gentle piano music)

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.350
Nearly identical to its
much more common cousin,

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.010
the Eastern cottontail,

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.630
the elusive New England
cottontail is found

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:24.340
only in a few isolated
pockets of its former habitat

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:27.600
that once ran from Maine to New York City.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.220
These rabbits have acute
eyesight and hearing.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.680
When they sense danger, they
will typically freeze in place,

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.713
relying on their gray-brown
fur to camouflage them.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:39.300
But when they need to run,

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:42.320
their powerful hunches allow
them to reach top speeds

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.530
of 18 miles per hour.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:46.940
But, unfortunately, their
speed can't save them

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:50.510
from invasive species
and a loss of habitat.

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:53.020
The New England
cottontail's very existence

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.250
now hangs in the balance.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.640
This is a New England cottontail rabbit.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:01.307
(playful music)

